hi this is presh talwalkar i'm going to  teach you a trick from vedic mathematics  so you can quickly square a number that  ends in the digit 5.  you'll be able to square this number  faster than you can do on a calculator  and you'll be able to do it in your head  let's say you want to do 25 squared  the trick is that just take the the  digit that's not 5  and multiply it by 1 more than itself  so 2 times 1 more than itself is 3  and you get the number 6.  then put the number 25 at the end  and that will be your answer 25 squared  is 625  we'll do another example  let's say you want to do 55 squared  we take the digit that's not 5  and we multiply it by one more than  itself  five times six is thirty  and so we get after adding the  twenty-five that fifty-five squared is  thirty-twenty-five  the general procedure is if you have a  number that ends in the digit 5  you take one more  than the number itself  you write that down  and you add the number 25 at the end  i like to end on this example to keep  students interested  205 we take 20  times 1 more than itself  and we get 420  25.  i hope you like this trick  please watch the video where i explain  why this works  you can catch me on my blog  bindyourdecisions  on twitter at preshtalwalker or get my  ebooks at amazon
 

